  "prefLabel": "Phy 201.01 Rules of Practice and Procedure",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Phy 201.01 Rules of Practice and Procedure. The Plc 200 rules shall govern with regards to all procedures for:\n\n(a) The receipt and investigation of misconduct complaints;\n\n(b) The conduct of adjudicative and non-adjudicative proceedings;\n\n(c) Rulemaking submissions, considerations, and dispositions of rulemaking petitions;\n\n(d) Public comment hearings;\n\n(e) Declaratory rulings;\n\n(f) Explanation of adopted rules;\n\n(g) Voluntary surrender of licenses; and\n\n(h) Waivers.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Phy 200) #12993, eff 2-22-20; ss by #14061, eff 8-21-24\n\nAPPENDIX\n\nRule | Statute\n\nPhy 200 | RSA 541-A:16, I(b)-(d)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/phy200.html"
